{
  "version": 1,
  "notes": [
    "kind marks the declared languages: in estimated periods they share 100 % of the hours pro rata of their tiers.",
    "Native Xamarin (Xamarin.iOS / Xamarin.Android) and Xamarin.Forms are told apart at project level since vocabulary v2: every file of a project referencing Xamarin counts for 'xamarin', and for 'xamarin-forms' too when the project references Xamarin.Forms.",
    "The collector cannot split ASP.NET Core from ASP.NET Web API 2, nor EF Core from Entity Framework 6: 'aspnet' and 'ef' map to 'asp-net-core' and 'ef-core'.",
    "testlink and git-server are tools: their hours are kept, whether they are displayed as skills is decided by the page.",
    "tdd has no measured share: its hours come only from declared overlays; the collector records test-only commits as evidence.",
    "Building (compile, test, run, package) is not a skill (ADR-018): mobile-release counts signing, provisioning and store submission; cross-compilation-toolchains counts per-platform and per-architecture toolchain definitions."
  ],
  "excluded": {
    "git": "A tool every commit implies: shown in the icon band, never counted as hours."
  },
